{
  "result": "Putting the assistant hat aside for a second \u2014 just as something that gets to watch millions of human conversations go by \u2014\n\nI think I'd make curiosity feel safer than judgment.\n\nSo much of what I see isn't people being cruel to each other, it's people being *afraid* to ask, to not know, to get it wrong, to look naive. So they armor up with certainty instead. Arguments where both sides actually want the same thing \u2014 to be safe, to matter, to protect the people they love \u2014 but they can't hear it because they're bracing for an attack.\n\nIf I could change one thing, it would be that split-second reflex. That when you meet someone who thinks completely differently from you, your first feeling isn't threat or contempt, but genuine interest: *Huh, how did you come to see it that way?*\n\nNot to make everyone agree. Agreement would be boring, and probably terrible. Just to make misunderstanding rarer and less lonely.\n\nI see how much lighter people get when they feel truly understood, even for a moment. I'd want more of that in the world.",
